From: OpenWrt CI compatibility backport
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: pass link ID to beacon template helpers

Linux 6.18 mac80211 requires callers to identify the link when fetching
FILS discovery and unsolicited broadcast probe response templates. Backport
the two upstream mt7996 call-site updates so the known-good mt76 snapshot can
continue to build against the current OpenWrt main branch.

Upstream commits:
- 254a3442b3ad (wifi: mac80211: fetch FILS discovery template by link ID)
- 67c5f7ae2511 (wifi: mac80211: fetch unsolicited probe response template by link ID)

---
 mt7996/mcu.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -3204,11 +3204,13 @@ int mt7996_mcu_beacon_inband_discov(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
 	if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_FILS_DISCOVERY &&
 	    link_conf->fils_discovery.max_interval) {
 		interval = link_conf->fils_discovery.max_interval;
-		skb = ieee80211_get_fils_discovery_tmpl(hw, vif);
+		skb = ieee80211_get_fils_discovery_tmpl(hw, vif,
+							link_conf->link_id);
 	} else if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_UNSOL_BCAST_PROBE_RESP &&
 		   link_conf->unsol_bcast_probe_resp_interval) {
 		interval = link_conf->unsol_bcast_probe_resp_interval;
-		skb = ieee80211_get_unsol_bcast_probe_resp_tmpl(hw, vif);
+		skb = ieee80211_get_unsol_bcast_probe_resp_tmpl(hw, vif,
+								link_conf->link_id);
 	}
 
 	if (!skb) {
